  "articleBody": "Getting the plumbing rough-in phase just right is super important for any remodel. Here's a quick checklist to make sure you're on track: First, make sure you've got those plumbing drawings and the overall project schedule aligned early on. This helps everyone understand the big picture. Next, it's crucial to confirm the scope of work and any exclusions in writing. This prevents surprises later. Before your plumber even steps on site, coordinate access and ensure all prerequisite work is complete. You don't want them waiting around! And if anything changes, make sure you use written change orders. This keeps everyone informed and accountable. Remember, plumbing rough-in typically happens after your building is dried in, and there are often trade-specific permits and inspections needed at various stages. Missing these steps can lead to frustrating delays. When you're tackling something like this, especially with multiple trades involved or specific inspection milestones, a professional coordinator like HH Remodeling LLC can really help streamline the process and make sure you're good to go.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}